{"cuisine/south-sudanese-cuisine":{"t":"cuisine","r":"cuisine/south-sudanese-cuisine","n":"South Sudanese cuisine","c":"#e46a3f","crumb":[["Africa","cuisines#africa"],["Cuisine"]],"sub":"National cuisine of S. Sudan","intro":[["South Sudanese cuisine is based on grains (maize, sorghum). It uses yams, potatoes, vegetables, legumes (beans, lentil, peanuts), meat (goat, mutton, chicken and fish near the rivers and lakes), okra and fruit as well. Meat is boiled, grilled or dried."],["South Sudanese cuisine was influenced by Arab cuisine."]],"src":"wikipedia","actions":[{"kind":"globe","hash":"south-sudanese-cuisine"},{"kind":"wiki","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/South_Sudanese_cuisine"}],"sections":[{"h":"Recipe sites","empty":"None yet","tryLinks":[]},{"h":"Cookbooks","count":1,"rows":[{"name":"South Sudanese Family Cookbook","color":"#f0b340","shape":"book","sub":"Jibrine Akima Magdaline Jok","note":"Self published collection of more than 100 South Sudanese family recipes, released in Melbourne around 2018.","url":"","suggested":true}]}],"cont":"African cuisine","img":{"src":"/labs/cuisines/img/thumb/6/69/Bowl_of_mandazi.jpg/500px-Bowl_of_mandazi.jpg","w":500,"h":333,"by":"The original uploader was ChildofMidnight at English Wikipedia.","lic":"CC BY 2.0","licUrl":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/2.0","page":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Bowl_of_mandazi.jpg"}},"cuisine/mexican-american-cuisine":{"t":"cuisine","r":"cuisine/mexican-american-cuisine","n":"Mexican-American cuisine","c":"#94bd5c","crumb":[["The Americas","cuisines#the-americas"],["Mexican cuisine","cuisine/mexican-cuisine"],["Fusion cuisine","cuisine/fusion-cuisine"]],"sub":"Diaspora cuisine in United States of America","intro":[["Mexican-American cuisine is the cuisine of Mexican Americans and their descendants, who have modified Mexican cuisine under the influence of American culture and immigration patterns of Mexicans to the United States."],["What many recognize as Mexican cuisine is the product of a storied fusion of cultures and flavors. Its culinary adaptability has impacted its spread and popularity on a global scale, and its presence in the United States is no exception. Culinary staples like tortillas, salsa, chips, chili, burritos, and tacos help to formulate many Americans' notions of Mexican food."],["Due in part to big business, immigration, and widespread likability, Mexican food and dishes have largely become regular constituents in American homes. While some of these popular iterations of Mexican food are far removed from their Mexican origins, they make up a large portion of the diets of many Americans. Additionally, more traditional Mexican cuisine has become increasingly common in the United States as it further diffuses to regions far from the U.S.-Mexico border."]],"src":"wikipedia","actions":[{"kind":"globe","hash":"mexican-american-cuisine"},{"kind":"wiki","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mexican-American_cuisine"}],"sections":[{"h":"Dishes","count":1,"links":[["White sauce (Virginia)","dish/white-sauce-virginia"]]},{"h":"Recipe sites","count":1,"rows":[{"name":"Muy Bueno","color":"#55b8ad","shape":"site","sub":"muybuenoblog.com","note":"Blog of Mexican-American family recipes.","url":"https://muybuenoblog.com/?p=24","suggested":true,"kind":"blog"}]},{"h":"Cookbooks","count":1,"rows":[{"name":"Chicano Eats: Recipes from My Mexican-American Kitchen","color":"#f0b340","shape":"book","sub":"Esteban Castillo, 2020","note":"Mexican-American home cooking from the creator of the Chicano Eats blog.","url":"https://openlibrary.org/isbn/9780062917379","suggested":true,"isbn":"9780062917379"}]},{"h":"Part of","links":[["Mexican cuisine","cuisine/mexican-cuisine"],["Fusion cuisine","cuisine/fusion-cuisine"]]},{"h":"Within Mexican-American cooking","count":4,"links":[["Cali-Mex cuisine","cuisine/cuisine-of-california-latino-and-hispanic-influence"],["Cali-Mex cuisine","cuisine/cali-mex-cuisine"],["New Mexican cuisine","cuisine/new-mexican-cuisine"],["Tex-Mex cuisine","cuisine/tex-mex-cuisine"]]}],"cont":"Cuisine of the Americas","img":{"src":"/labs/cuisines/img/thumb/b/b2/CornmealProducts.jpg/500px-CornmealProducts.jpg","w":500,"h":769,"by":"Scott Bauer","lic":"Public domain","licUrl":"","page":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:CornmealProducts.jpg"}},"ingredient/dried-shrimp":{"t":"ingredient","r":"ingredient/dried-shrimp","n":"Dried shrimp","c":"#c9b8dd","crumb":[["Ingredients","ingredients"]],"sub":"Ingredient in 5 dishes across 2 cuisines","intro":[["Dried shrimp are shrimp that have been sun-dried and shrunk to a thumbnail size. They are used in many African, East Asian, Southeast Asian and South Asian cuisines, imparting a unique umami taste. A handful of shrimp is generally used for dishes. The flavors of this ingredient are released when allowed to simmer."]],"src":"wikipedia","actions":[{"kind":"globe","hash":"ingredient-dried-shrimp"},{"kind":"wiki","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Dried_shrimp"}],"sections":[{"h":"Where it's cooked with","count":2,"groups":[["Indonesian cuisine","cuisine/indonesian-cuisine",[["Bubur pedas","dish/bubur-pedas"],["Kerak telor","dish/kerak-telor"],["Lumpia semarang","dish/lumpia-semarang"],["Mie celor","dish/mie-celor"]]],["Thai cuisine","cuisine/thai-cuisine",[["Pad thai","dish/pad-thai"]]]]},{"h":"Often cooked with","links":[["Ginger","ingredient/ginger"],["Egg","ingredient/egg"],["Shrimp","ingredient/shrimp"],["Bamboo shoot","ingredient/bamboo-shoot"],["Chili pepper","ingredient/chili-pepper"],["Garlic","ingredient/garlic"],["Shallots","ingredient/shallots"],["Mung bean sprout","ingredient/mung-bean-sprout"],["Anchovy","ingredient/anchovy"],["Bean curd","ingredient/bean-curd"],["Bumbu (seasoning)","ingredient/bumbu-seasoning"],["Caraway seed","ingredient/caraway-seed"],["Carrots","ingredient/carrots"],["Coconut","ingredient/coconut"],["Galangal","ingredient/galangal"],["Leafy greens","ingredient/leafy-greens"]]}],"img":{"src":"/labs/cuisines/img/thumb/2/22/Dried_river_shrimp.JPG/500px-Dried_river_shrimp.JPG","w":500,"h":333,"by":"Humanfeather / Michelle Jo","lic":"CC BY 3.0","licUrl":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/3.0","page":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Dried_river_shrimp.JPG"}},"ingredient/hollandaise-sauce":{"t":"ingredient","r":"ingredient/hollandaise-sauce","n":"Hollandaise sauce","c":"#c9b8dd","crumb":[["Ingredients","ingredients"]],"sub":"Ingredient in 1 dish across 1 cuisine","intro":[["Hollandaise sauce is a French recipe,  a mixture of egg yolk, melted butter, and lemon juice (or a white wine or vinegar reduction). It is usually seasoned with salt, and either white pepper or cayenne pepper."]],"src":"wikipedia","actions":[{"kind":"globe","hash":"ingredient-hollandaise-sauce"},{"kind":"wiki","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Hollandaise_sauce"}],"sections":[{"h":"Where it's cooked with","count":1,"groups":[["Louisiana Creole cuisine","cuisine/louisiana-creole-cuisine",[["Eggs Sardou","dish/eggs-sardou"]]]]},{"h":"Often cooked with","links":[["Artichoke","ingredient/artichoke"],["Egg","ingredient/egg"],["Engraulis","ingredient/engraulis"],["Poached egg","ingredient/poached-egg"],["Spinach","ingredient/spinach"],["Tuber","ingredient/tuber"]]}],"img":{"src":"/labs/cuisines/img/thumb/e/ef/Hollandaise_sauce.jpg/500px-Hollandaise_sauce.jpg","w":500,"h":333,"by":"Mark Miller","lic":"CC BY-SA 4.0","licUrl":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0","page":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Hollandaise_sauce.jpg"}},"dish/fraisier":{"t":"dish","r":"dish/fraisier","n":"Fraisier","c":"#ede6da","crumb":[["Dishes","dishes"]],"sub":"Dish found in 2 cuisines","dot":"#cf5f87","intro":[["The fraisier is a strawberry cake made of an almond sponge cake or meringue, pastry cream, and strawberries. The pastry is typically made during strawberry season, as the crucial ingredient is the strawberries. The name derives from the French word for strawberries, fraises. It is a classic among French entremet desserts. According to the New York Times, the required construction is often elaborate."]],"src":"wikipedia","actions":[{"kind":"globe","hash":"dish-fraisier"},{"kind":"wiki","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Fraisier"}],"sections":[{"h":"Where it's from","links":[["French cuisine","cuisine/french-cuisine"],["New Caledonian cuisine","cuisine/new-caledonian-cuisine"]]},{"h":"Ingredients","count":3,"links":[["Cream","ingredient/cream"],["Custard","ingredient/custard"],["Genoise","ingredient/genoise"]]},{"h":"Cook it","rows":[{"name":"Pardon Your French","color":"#55b8ad","shape":"site","sub":"pardonyourfrench.com","note":"Audrey Le Goff, a French cook, shares classic and regional French home recipes.","url":"https://pardonyourfrench.com","suggested":true,"kind":"blog"},{"name":"La Cuisine de Géraldine","color":"#55b8ad","shape":"site","sub":"lacuisinedegeraldine.fr","note":"French home cooking blog by Géraldine Leverd, also author of The New French Kitchen.","url":"https://lacuisinedegeraldine.fr/en/about-us","suggested":true,"kind":"blog"},{"name":"New Caledonia Tourism: Kanak cooking","color":"#55b8ad","shape":"site","sub":"newcaledonia.travel","note":"Official tourism board overview of Kanak food, including bougna cooked in an earth oven.","url":"https://www.newcaledonia.travel/nz/gastronomy-wine/gastronomy/kanak-cooking","suggested":true,"kind":"site"}]},{"h":"More from French cuisine","links":[["Adventureland Bazaar","dish/adventureland-bazaar"],["Albufera sauce","dish/albufera-sauce"],["Andouillette","dish/andouillette"],["Aspic","dish/aspic"],["Bayonne ham","dish/bayonne-ham"],["Beef Stroganoff","dish/beef-stroganoff"],["Beurre maître d'hôtel","dish/beurre-maitre-d-hotel"],["Beurre manié","dish/beurre-manie"],["Bisque (food)","dish/bisque-food"],["Blanquette de veau","dish/blanquette-de-veau"],["Blini","dish/blini"],["Bolinhos de bacalhau","dish/bolinhos-de-bacalhau"],["Bouillabaisse","dish/bouillabaisse"],["Bourride","dish/bour